    Represents the ideal M_k = (x_i | i != k) + (1 + x_k).
    In our Boolean ring, M_k is a maximal (and thus prime) ideal.
    Since every prime ideal in a Boolean ring is minimal over (0),
    M_k is a minimal prime ideal over (0).
